(932993, 107733, 24065, '<td valign="top">The colors in this photo are beautiful.  There were 2 things that I thought would improve the photo.  So, for whatever it''s worth.... the horizontal division is distracting to me; I felt a solid color covering floor &amp; wall would have helped.  And, the pan right in the middle was not appealing.  If it had been placed on one of the thirds - I would prefer the upper right - I think it would have drawn the eye into the photo.   I did not rate this low, just wanted you to know why I didn''t rate it as high as some.</td>', 'The colors in this photo are beautiful.  There were 2 things that I thought would improve the photo.  So, for whatever it''s worth.... the horizontal division is distracting to me; I felt a solid color covering floor & wall would have helped.  And, the pan right in the middle was not appealing.  If it had been placed on one of the thirds - I would prefer the upper right - I think it would have drawn the eye into the photo.   I did not rate this low, just wanted you to know why I didn''t rate it as high as some.', '2004-09-30 16:54:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(932994, 107502, 24065, '<td valign="top">I loved your idea.  It is well focused, very creative and I like the tile background.  But there seems to be some kind of haze over the picture -- it lacks clarity.  I don''t know enough to tell you what caused it, but can definitely see it -- even on the thumbnails.  (I checked on 3 different monitors.)  I didn''t rate it low, but did rate a couple of others higher because of that.  Still, it really made me chuckle!</td>', 'I loved your idea.  It is well focused, very creative and I like the tile background.  But there seems to be some kind of haze over the picture -- it lacks clarity.  I don''t know enough to tell you what caused it, but can definitely see it -- even on the thumbnails.  (I checked on 3 different monitors.)  I didn''t rate it low, but did rate a couple of others higher because of that.  Still, it really made me chuckle!', '2004-09-30 16:56:59.000000', NULL, 1),
