(944275, 108592, 17203, '<td valign="top">Y''know, I''m a little surprised this placed as well as it did. The mass of "stuff" in the center of the image is just too busy for my taste, but that''s what I get for waiting until the last minute. I''ll bet a single roll (with lots of legs) held between the chopsticks would have worked much better. I also blew the contrast (as crabappl3 correctly pointed out) by not viewing the entry on a CRT- the background is totally black on a good LCD monitor. Still, I''m doing a major happy dance for finally reaching my goal of 6 for a profile average. Woohoo! :-D<br/> <br/>FWIW- Like many spiders, I did eat my subject after the fun was over.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-10-06 00:55:27.</i></td>', 'Y''know, I''m a little surprised this placed as well as it did. The mass of "stuff" in the center of the image is just too busy for my taste, but that''s what I get for waiting until the last minute. I''ll bet a single roll (with lots of legs) held between the chopsticks would have worked much better. I also blew the contrast (as crabappl3 correctly pointed out) by not viewing the entry on a CRT- the background is totally black on a good LCD monitor. Still, I''m doing a major happy dance for finally reaching my goal of 6 for a profile average. Woohoo! :-D FWIW- Like many spiders, I did eat my subject after the fun was over.', '2004-10-06 01:24:48.000000', '2004-10-06 01:55:27.000000', 0),
