(944794, 107916, 22011, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments folks.<br/> <br/>I''d like to thank the fish for the 20th placing... :-).<br/> <br/>I think NZ is the only place you can get the fish, I did a bit of travelling in a previous job and never saw them anywhere..<br/> <br/>If you''re a ExPat Kiwi and want a couple sent over, PM me and I''ll post em. :-).<br/> <br/>Edit: 4 in the top 20?  I think we need to wrangle a kiwi top three effort somehow. Maybe a challenge requiring photos of hokey-pokey icecream, Jaffas and Chocolate fish?<br/> <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-10-06 03:40:52.</i></td>', 'Thanks for all the comments folks. I''d like to thank the fish for the 20th placing... :-). I think NZ is the only place you can get the fish, I did a bit of travelling in a previous job and never saw them anywhere.. If you''re a ExPat Kiwi and want a couple sent over, PM me and I''ll post em. :-). Edit: 4 in the top 20?  I think we need to wrangle a kiwi top three effort somehow. Maybe a challenge requiring photos of hokey-pokey icecream, Jaffas and Chocolate fish? ', '2004-10-06 04:37:25.000000', '2004-10-06 04:40:52.000000', 0),
(944821, 107916, 24983, '<td valign="top">I figured on the kiwi connection the wild appitite is a favorite of mine. have you tried the GIANT Jaffas on sale at New World, congrat on the placing I rated it highly. BTW my son in Japan misses Marmite, and timtams and weetbix, so we have to keep posting food parcels from home. Oh the expense goes on even when they leave home!!!!!!!!</td>', 'I figured on the kiwi connection the wild appitite is a favorite of mine. have you tried the GIANT Jaffas on sale at New World, congrat on the placing I rated it highly. BTW my son in Japan misses Marmite, and timtams and weetbix, so we have to keep posting food parcels from home. Oh the expense goes on even when they leave home!!!!!!!!', '2004-10-06 05:07:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(944826, 108603, 27524, '<td valign="top">Congratulations... it was truly one of the best idea in challenge.</td>', 'Congratulations... it was truly one of the best idea in challenge.', '2004-10-06 05:18:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(944831, 107798, 25486, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get a chance to vote during the challenge, sorry.  I think the shot is very good technically.  The DOF is ok, defining the look you were after as you said.  The composition is good, the knife is carefully placed.  If anything it looks a bit too "staged" if you see what I mean?  There''s no crumbs at all, the knife clean and polished.  I agree with crabappl3, one or two jelly babies on the plate may have helped the idea along a bit?<br/> <br/>Also, I''m no expert on lighting, not by any stretch of the imagination, but it seems a bit dull or flat, whatever the expression should be.  I do know that the right light can make a or break a shot, I''m not saying it broken this one but it seems to lack some lustre, if that makes any sense and was of any help then you''re welcome, if not then forget it, if you like it the way it is then that''s what counts.</td>', 'I didn''t get a chance to vote during the challenge, sorry.  I think the shot is very good technically.  The DOF is ok, defining the look you were after as you said.  The composition is good, the knife is carefully placed.  If anything it looks a bit too "staged" if you see what I mean?  There''s no crumbs at all, the knife clean and polished.  I agree with crabappl3, one or two jelly babies on the plate may have helped the idea along a bit? Also, I''m no expert on lighting, not by any stretch of the imagination, but it seems a bit dull or flat, whatever the expression should be.  I do know that the right light can make a or break a shot, I''m not saying it broken this one but it seems to lack some lustre, if that makes any sense and was of any help then you''re welcome, if not then forget it, if you like it the way it is then that''s what counts.', '2004-10-06 05:21:55.000000', NULL, 0),
