(945872, 108588, 22781, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club Comment: </b> <br/> <br/>Hi there, <br/> <br/>So, here I am again<br/> <br/>Just finished on your complexity entry, pushed the button and got this one to critique Guess that doesnt happen much.<br/>Ive read in your profile that you want to score 8+ photos at least 3 ribbons within 3 months and a 6+ overall score, so to achieve that I am not going to be nice, but realy point out why you didnt win (in my opinion) instead of being nice and say that your photo is not so bad. <br/>Your photo isnt so bad, but its far from a ribbon, and if thats what you want well. Hold on for the negative comments that follw :-)<br/>I also commented on this one in the challenge.<br/>OK, so now I am going to try to help you here to win the next challenge (not the free study, Im going to win that)<br/> <br/>Lets take the Handburger (same idea) as a point of reference and see how you could improve<br/> <br/>As you have seen from the comments your photo is a bit blue-ish , there is a simple way to overcome this problem.<br/>Here is a simple but effective tutorial how to do this in Photoshop.<br/><a href="//www.idigitalemotion.com/tutorials/guest/colorfix/colorfix.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.idigitalemotion.com/tutorials/guest/colorfix/colorfix.html</a> <br/>Your composition is also not really flattering, its funny but not really convincing. You filled the entire frame leaving you with an almost centered composition. Try to make use of the rule of thirds:<br/><a href="//www.aea1.k12.ia.us/lois/ruleofthirds.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.aea1.k12.ia.us/lois/ruleofthirds.html</a> <br/>And as you can see people here at DPC really like negative space, so theres nothing wrong with using that.<br/> <br/>Furthermore the hand is a bit washed out and has some ugly highlights (from the flash?) the glass and the plate also have some nasty reflections.<br/> <br/>Just go to buy some 1000watt work lights (2 of them or so) and experiment with lighting. The reflections on the glass and plate could been taken care of with a polarizer..<br/> <br/>Well thats all I have to say for now, hope you are not to mad at me.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work. <br/> <br/>If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or are bored and want to spam someone just PM me. <br/> <br/>Grrrtzzz<br/>Peter/CC<br/></td>', 'Critique Club Comment:   Hi there,  So, here I am again Just finished on your complexity entry, pushed the button and got this one to critique Guess that doesnt happen much.Ive read in your profile that you want to score 8+ photos at least 3 ribbons within 3 months and a 6+ overall score, so to achieve that I am not going to be nice, but realy point out why you didnt win (in my opinion) instead of being nice and say that your photo is not so bad. Your photo isnt so bad, but its far from a ribbon, and if thats what you want well. Hold on for the negative comments that follw :-)I also commented on this one in the challenge.OK, so now I am going to try to help you here to win the next challenge (not the free study, Im going to win that) Lets take the Handburger (same idea) as a point of reference and see how you could improve As you have seen from the comments your photo is a bit blue-ish , there is a simple way to overcome this problem.Here is a simple but effective tutorial how to do this in Photoshop.//www.idigitalemotion.com/tutorials/guest/colorfix/colorfix.html Your composition is also not really flattering, its funny but not really convincing. You filled the entire frame leaving you with an almost centered composition. Try to make use of the rule of thirds://www.aea1.k12.ia.us/lois/ruleofthirds.html And as you can see people here at DPC really like negative space, so theres nothing wrong with using that. Furthermore the hand is a bit washed out and has some ugly highlights (from the flash?) the glass and the plate also have some nasty reflections. Just go to buy some 1000watt work lights (2 of them or so) and experiment with lighting. The reflections on the glass and plate could been taken care of with a polarizer.. Well thats all I have to say for now, hope you are not to mad at me. Keep up the good work.  If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or are bored and want to spam someone just PM me.  GrrrtzzzPeter/CC', '2004-10-06 14:59:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(946194, 107651, 1031, '<td valign="top">I also took a shot of some maize, but decided to enter something else. From the look of your finish I should have entered the corn!<br/> <br/>When I was a kid I took some and planted it and grew quite a bit -- this kind gets 6-8 feet high; most of the ears would come out multicolored, but a few would be a beautiful solid red or purple. One or two ears is enough to sow a sizable plot.</td>', 'I also took a shot of some maize, but decided to enter something else. From the look of your finish I should have entered the corn! When I was a kid I took some and planted it and grew quite a bit -- this kind gets 6-8 feet high; most of the ears would come out multicolored, but a few would be a beautiful solid red or purple. One or two ears is enough to sow a sizable plot.', '2004-10-06 16:30:58.000000', NULL, 0),
