(946781, 107383, 93, '<td valign="top">Thank you to everyone that took the time to comment on my entry.  Many of you kind of gave me a bit of validation for my first real attempt at studio work, and that''s always great :)<br/> <br/>I also really like my title, for that one person that suggested I needed a new one. It''s a social commentary on the state of our children today and what they are being fed to start their mornings (in many cases), and the title is there to reflect the band-aid method we use to control what we''ve caused. Feed them sugar, then dope them up when it starts to effect them.<br/> <br/>Social commentary, however, generally isn''t the best thing on DPC.. but when a person has and idea...<br/> <br/>Anyway, thanks again everyone. 32nd place is definitely nothing to sniff at :)</td>', 'Thank you to everyone that took the time to comment on my entry.  Many of you kind of gave me a bit of validation for my first real attempt at studio work, and that''s always great :) I also really like my title, for that one person that suggested I needed a new one. It''s a social commentary on the state of our children today and what they are being fed to start their mornings (in many cases), and the title is there to reflect the band-aid method we use to control what we''ve caused. Feed them sugar, then dope them up when it starts to effect them. Social commentary, however, generally isn''t the best thing on DPC.. but when a person has and idea... Anyway, thanks again everyone. 32nd place is definitely nothing to sniff at :)', '2004-10-06 21:03:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(946784, 108512, 20941, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your first ribbon, more to come I expect. This is a great entry, humerous, pleasing to look at, great creativity!</td>', 'Congratulations on your first ribbon, more to come I expect. This is a great entry, humerous, pleasing to look at, great creativity!', '2004-10-06 21:04:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(946795, 108504, 25742, '<td valign="top">This was actually quite difficult shot to get. I hadn''t come up with any good idea for the challenge and was gonna let it go past untouched. BUT, then I remembered the dried fishheads, and drove of to a place with nice BG, but no fishheads there anymore. o-oh. Then I remembered this place, on the way to Krýsuvík, just out of Hafnafjörður and hurried over there, because it was already late on the last day of challenge submissions. When I got there all the fishheads were on these wooden racks, about 3-4m above me. Fortunately I had with me my monster tripod (I think it can be used to steady Scud missiles) and my remote control so I could raise the camera up to the max height and shoot with the remote. I was aiming for deep DOF and hoping for the other fishheads appearing in the BG, with low shutter speed and small apperture. Now the light started to fade a lot and it was overcast and likely to start to rain. So shutter speeds to 15-30 sec and hope. Did I mention the smell? And the yukkie fishgutter ground? No, better not. Don''t try to imagine it, just take my word for it - I''m not going there again. Finally I found some fishheads that weren''t too high and shot this. <br/>I agree with many commentators that the BG is distracting, esp the big white bits.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-07-30 12:03:29.</i></td>', 'This was actually quite difficult shot to get. I hadn''t come up with any good idea for the challenge and was gonna let it go past untouched. BUT, then I remembered the dried fishheads, and drove of to a place with nice BG, but no fishheads there anymore. o-oh. Then I remembered this place, on the way to Krýsuvík, just out of Hafnafjörður and hurried over there, because it was already late on the last day of challenge submissions. When I got there all the fishheads were on these wooden racks, about 3-4m above me. Fortunately I had with me my monster tripod (I think it can be used to steady Scud missiles) and my remote control so I could raise the camera up to the max height and shoot with the remote. I was aiming for deep DOF and hoping for the other fishheads appearing in the BG, with low shutter speed and small apperture. Now the light started to fade a lot and it was overcast and likely to start to rain. So shutter speeds to 15-30 sec and hope. Did I mention the smell? And the yukkie fishgutter ground? No, better not. Don''t try to imagine it, just take my word for it - I''m not going there again. Finally I found some fishheads that weren''t too high and shot this. I agree with many commentators that the BG is distracting, esp the big white bits.', '2004-10-06 21:09:50.000000', '2005-07-30 13:03:29.000000', 0),
